34:| Finite-quiver stability and Hall wall crossing | `library/hall-algebras-and-tensor-categories/hall-stability-dt-bps-and-wall-crossing.md` (`hall-stability-dt-bps-and-wall-crossing`): `def-finite-acyclic-quiver-stability-data`, `lem-finite-acyclic-quiver-representations-are-finitary-hereditary-with-euler-form`, `lem-upper-half-plane-sum-phase-between`, `lem-quiver-hardernarasimhan-filtrations-exist-are-unique-and-descend`, `def-subobject-first-completed-finite-quiver-hall-algebra-and-tori`, `thm-finite-quiver-euler-and-skew-integration-is-multiplicative`, `thm-finite-quiver-hall-wall-crossing`, and `rem-finite-quiver-hall-counts-and-dt-bps-interpretation`. | This is a precise finite-field, finite-acyclic-quiver Hall/HN construction; its source page explicitly says it is not Behrend-weighted CY3 DT, motivic vanishing-cycle integration, cohomological BPS spaces or physical state counting. The theorem carrier is tagged `published` and contains a local proof, but the visible frontmatter has only `verification.precheck: pass`; bind the actual acceptance evidence before treating the current file as a certified proof supplier. |
35:| QFT-local Hall spectrum generator | `physics/library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-hall-bps-wall-crossing.md` (`qftx-hall-bps-wall-crossing`) and its examples page `qftx-hall-bps-wall-crossing-examples`. Exact items are `def-qftx-hall-spectrum-generator`, `prop-qftx-hall-spectrum-invariance`, and `def-qftx-cy3-bps-integration-contract`, all `domain: mathematics`, `library: mathematics`. The generator is defined for finite acyclic quivers over `F_q`; the invariance proposition uses `thm-finite-quiver-hall-wall-crossing`; the bridge item is a definition of required input data. The first two items have delegated verification dated 2026-10-22; the bridge is also source-reviewed/verified in that run. | This is the strongest exact reuse interface for the new category's quiver wall-crossing prose. `P_Z^E` and `P_Z^sk` are formal products in a dimension completion; no analytic convergence or physical state-counting is asserted. `def-qftx-cy3-bps-integration-contract` lists the extra CY3/category, stability, orientation, completed Hall/CoHA integration and physical Hilbert-supertrace comparison required for any bridge. It explicitly does not assert that such a package exists or that arbitrary Hall modules are BPS spaces. |
36:| Quiver CoHA and motivic constructions | `physics/library/hall-algebras-and-tensor-categories/cohomological-hall-algebras-and-quiver-correspondences.md` (`cohomological-hall-algebras-and-quiver-correspondences`): `def-quiver-representation-stacks-and-exact-sequence-correspondences`, `thm-quiver-quotient-stack-borel-moore-operation-package`, `def-untwisted-quiver-cohomological-hall-algebra`, `thm-untwisted-quiver-coha-is-associative-and-unital`, `def-quiver-potential-and-monodromic-vanishing-cycle-data`, `def-critical-quiver-coha-from-vanishing-cycle-data`, `thm-critical-quiver-coha-associative-under-coherence-axioms`, and related lemmas. Also `physics/library/hall-algebras-and-tensor-categories/motivic-hall-algebras-and-integration.md` (`motivic-hall-algebras-and-integration`): `def-motivic-hall-algebra-of-a-finite-quiver`, `def-quiver-motivic-quantum-torus`, `thm-quiver-motivic-hall-convolution-associative`, `thm-quiver-motivic-integration-is-multiplicative`. | These pages define equivariant quotient-stack Borel–Moore operations and finite-quiver Hall constructions. They are specialized to the stated quotient stacks, coefficient systems and operations; the CoHA page explicitly does not identify them with physical BPS Hilbert spaces. The local CoHA page excludes mixed-Hodge enrichment and off-shell rapid-decay cohomology. This equivariant Borel–Moore theory is not the missing smooth-manifold Borel/Cartan theory or a general localization theorem. |
42:## Smallest missing mathematical suppliers
50:| `def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model` | definition | For a compact torus `T` acting smoothly on a manifold `M`, define the Borel space `ET×_T M`, `H_T^*(M;R)`, the coefficient ring `H_T^*(pt;R)=Sym(t^*)` with degree-two generators, and the Cartan complex `(Sym(t^*)⊗Ω(M))^T` with `d_T=d-Σu_i ι_{X_i}`. Prove `d_T^2=0` on invariants. If using the Cartan model as a computational substitute, prove/cite the comparison for the declared compact-connected group and coefficients; do not conflate rational Borel cohomology, real Cartan cohomology, equivariant Chow groups and quotient-stack Borel–Moore homology. |
51:| `thm-borel-localization-for-compact-torus-actions` | theorem | For a compact smooth `T`-manifold and rational or real coefficients, define the multiplicative set generated by nonzero characters of `T`. Prove restriction to the fixed locus `M^T` becomes an isomorphism after that localization, with its precise compactness/finite-type hypotheses. The proof needs the fixed-set submanifold, a `T`-invariant tubular neighborhood, the equivariant Thom/Gysin map and the fact that each normal weight is invertible in the localized coefficient ring. On the complement, give a finite orbit-type/slice cover; each proper isotropy subgroup has a nonzero character vanishing on its identity component, so its equivariant cohomology is torsion after localization. State separately any properness/compact-support version for noncompact spaces. |
