library/mathematical-statistics/symmetrization-rademacher-complexity-and-covering-entropy.md:31:The Rademacher complexity here is one-sided and has no absolute value. Coordinate contraction has factor $L$ without requiring the coordinate maps to vanish at zero. The separate absolute-value theorem assumes they do vanish at zero and has factor $2L$. For a finite class of $[0,1]$-valued functions, the uniform deviation bound is $2|\mathcal F|e^{-2n\epsilon^2}$.
