library/hopf-hecke-algebras/quasitriangular-hopf-algebras-and-braided-module-categories.md:15:This page works over a field with algebraic tensor products and the category of all left modules. It fixes the leg embeddings and canonical associators before defining a quasitriangular structure. The universal tensor is always a finite element of $H\otimes H$; the Yang–Baxter equation follows from the first hexagon together with the coproduct-intertwining axiom $R\Delta(h)=\Delta^{\mathrm{op}}(h)R$, using the Hopf structure. It cannot replace these quasitriangular axioms. A braiding on all modules determines the algebraic tensor using naturality on the regular module, with no finite-dimensionality assumption.
