library/hopf-hecke-algebras/hopf-hecke-and-quantum-symmetry-interfaces.md:44:[[def-hh-rational-spectral-r-matrix]] fixes the two-dimensional rational family $R(u)=uI+iP$ and its checked operator. [[lem-hh-rational-spectral-r-matrix-satisfies-yang-baxter]] proves both the un-checked parameterized Yang–Baxter equation and its checked braid-form identity by a direct $S_3$ operator calculation. The item concerns finite-dimensional vector spaces; it is not a universal Hopf $R$-matrix or a braiding on a category of affine modules. Full RTT, arbitrary spectral transfer matrices, and all-type evaluation-module claims remain outside this local result.
library/complex-analysis/hodge-theory-on-compact-riemann-surfaces-examples.md:14:These examples distinguish smooth Dolbeault cohomology from its metric-dependent harmonic representatives. The square torus supplies a nonzero exact form that cannot be harmonic. On every compact connected curve the degree-zero harmonic functions of the trivial bundle are constants. A varying Hermitian weight on a flat torus changes the degree-one harmonic space, with an explicit normalized representative for the same cohomology class. The sphere has no holomorphic differential and therefore has vanishing degree-one Dolbeault cohomology; a flat torus has one-dimensional cohomology represented by its descended constant form.
