## Definition

Let $T=(\mathbb R/\mathbb Z)^r$ be a compact torus with a fixed product
presentation, and let $M$ be a smooth manifold without boundary, not assumed
compact, with a smooth left action $a:T\times M\to M$. Work over $\mathbb R$
and use the chosen product Milnor model $ET=(E_{S^1})^r$ and $BT=ET/T$ from
the preceding coefficient lemma. Give $ET\times M$ the right diagonal action
$(e,p)\cdot t=(e\cdot t,t^{-1}\cdot p)$ and define
$$ET\times_T M:=(ET\times M)/T.$$
The **Borel equivariant cohomology** is the graded ring
$$H_T^*(M;\mathbb R):=H_{\mathrm{sing}}^*(ET\times_T M;\mathbb R).$$
For $M=\{\ast\}$ this gives $H_T^*(\ast;\mathbb R)=H^*(BT;\mathbb R)$;
the selected degree-two normalization in
$\operatorname{Sym}_{\mathbb R}(\mathfrak t^*)$ is the isomorphism established
in the preceding coefficient lemma.

The quotient map $q:ET\times M\to ET\times_T M$ and projection
$\pi([e,p])=[e]$ give the associated-space square
$$
\begin{tikzcd}
ET\times M \arrow[r,"q"] \arrow[d,"\operatorname{pr}_1"'] & ET\times_T M \arrow[d,"\pi"]\\
ET \arrow[r,"q_T"'] & BT
\end{tikzcd}
$$
where $q_T:ET\to BT$ is the orbit quotient. The square commutes because both
composites send $(e,p)$ to $[e]$.

Let $\mathfrak t=T_eT$, with basis $e_1,\ldots,e_r$ and dual basis
$u_1,\ldots,u_r$. Regard $\operatorname{Sym}_{\mathbb R}(\mathfrak t^*)$ as a
polynomial algebra by assigning each linear generator degree two. The induced
left action of $T$ on forms is $t\cdot\alpha=(a_{t^{-1}})^*\alpha$; its
coadjoint action on $\mathfrak t^*$ is trivial because $T$ is abelian. The
**Cartan complex** is the graded-commutative algebra
$$C_T(M):=\bigl(\operatorname{Sym}_{\mathbb R}(\mathfrak t^*)\otimes_{\mathbb R}\Omega^*(M)\bigr)^T,$$
where the superscript denotes the fixed subspace for the diagonal action and a
polynomial of degree $j$ tensored with a $k$-form has total degree $2j+k$. For
$\xi\in\mathfrak t$, use the library fundamental vector field
$$X_\xi(p)=\left.\frac{d}{ds}\right|_{s=0}\exp_T(-s\xi)\cdot p.$$
On polynomial-valued forms define the degree-one Cartan operator
$$d_T(P\otimes\alpha)=P\otimes d\alpha-\sum_{i=1}^r(u_iP)\otimes\iota_{X_{e_i}}\alpha,$$
extended linearly. The tensor $\sum_i u_i\otimes X_{e_i}$ is basis-independent.
The **Cartan equivariant cohomology** in this item means
$H^*(C_T(M),d_T)$; the proof below establishes $d_T^2=0$ on $C_T(M)$.

This definition does not assert a general isomorphism between the Borel and
Cartan cohomology rings. It defines neither equivariant Chow groups nor
equivariant quotient-stack Borel–Moore homology, and no rational-coefficient
comparison is being used in the real Cartan complex.

