        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $T=M=\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z$, with $T$ acting on $M$ by left translation $t\\cdot[x]=[t+x]$. Use the period-one tangent generator $e$, so the library convention gives $X_e=-\\partial_x$, and let $\\eta$ be the global one-form on $\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z$ descended from $-dx$ on $\\mathbb R$. In the chosen Borel model the map $[v,x]\\mapsto v\\cdot x$ identifies $ET\\times_TT$ with $ET$, hence $H_T^0(T;\\mathbb R)=\\mathbb R$ and $H_T^k(T;\\mathbb R)=0$ for $k>0$. The invariant Cartan complex is $\\mathbb R[u]\\oplus\\mathbb R[u]\\eta$, with $|u|=2$, $|\\eta|=1$, $d_TP(u)=0$, and $d_T(P(u)\\eta)=-uP(u)$. Its cohomology is $\\mathbb R$ in degree zero and zero in positive degrees, agreeing with the Borel calculation for this action.",
