+# Batch 7 authoring notes
+
+Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`  
+Pair: `qftx-equivariant-cohomology` / `qftx-equivariant-cohomology-examples`  
+Batch dependency level: 0 (`advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json` lists no in-run batch supplier for batch 7).
+
+## Plan comparison and prerequisite review
+
+The full design section and `research/plan-spec.json` agree on the pair IDs,
+category, mathematics library, title, companion, and the page prerequisite
+`moment-maps-and-symplectic-reduction`. The plan and batch manifest currently
+have empty item arrays, while the design and its proposed inventory name
+`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model`; the empty arrays are the
+authoring placeholders described in the scaffold, not a scope conflict. The
+design limits the A page to a compact torus, its Borel construction and Cartan
+complex, and a local proof that $d_T^2=0$ on invariants. It does not require the
+general Borel–Cartan comparison or any localization theorem.
+
+The research note identifies the moment-map page as a source of smooth group
+actions, moment-map language and the library fundamental-field sign. Its actual
+items do not supply Borel or Cartan cohomology. The proposed inventory lists
+`def-symplectic-and-hamiltonian-lie-group-action` and
+`def-moment-map-and-component-hamiltonian` as inactive, nonlogical candidates;
+their Hamiltonian hypotheses are not prerequisites for this smooth-action
+definition. The authored item instead uses the exact general fundamental-field
+interface and retains the required page edge. The named definition
+`def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model` is supplemented by the local
+lemma `lem-torus-classifying-space-cohomology`: the coefficient-ring identity
+$H^*(BT;\mathbb R)\cong\operatorname{Sym}(\mathfrak t^*)$ needs its own proof.
+
+Before authoring, `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision` were run for the listed
+external mathematical candidates and the inspected mathematical suppliers.
+They report `Readiness record missing` because those published root items are
+not owned by this run's manifests or plan. This is not treated as an in-run
+readiness gap: the actual imported statements and proofs were inspected, their
+current carrier hashes match `research/math-imports.json`, and their current
+verification fields are recorded in the item source files. No supplier is
+escalated merely for lacking a Step 1 row in this physics run.
+
+## Completed item checkpoint: `lem-torus-classifying-space-cohomology`
+
+**Claim and conventions.** For a fixed product presentation
+$T=(\mathbb R/\mathbb Z)^r$, the product Milnor model gives
+$BT\cong(\mathbb{CP}^{\infty})^r$ and
+$H^*(BT;\mathbb R)\cong\mathbb R[u_1,\ldots,u_r]$ with degree-two generators
+identified with the dual period-one Lie-algebra basis. The proof explicitly
+uses AC through the cited projective-space, universal-coefficient, and Künneth
